  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DEVELOPMENT OF SYSTEMS AND METHODS FOR THE ASSESSMENT AND CONSERVATION OF CHIQUIBUL-MAYA MOUNTAINS BIOSPHERE RESERVE&apos;S WILDLIFE AND HABITATS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO DEVELOP AND REFINE SYSTEMS TO IMPROVE MONITORING AND PROMOTE ENVIRONMENTAL EDUCATION WITHIN THE POPULATION OF THE CHIQUIBUL-MAYA MOUNTAINS BIOSPHERE RESERVE IN GUATEMALA AND BELIZE TO ORDER TO INCREASE CROSS-BORDER COOPERATION IN WILDLIFE AND HABITAT CONSERVATION. THE PROJECT IS INTENDED TO CONSERVE EMBLEMATIC SPECIES SUCH AS JAGUARS (PANTHERA ONCA), BAIRD S TAPIR (TAPIRUS BAIRDII), AND SCARLET MACAWS (ARA MACAO) BY ADDRESSING THE IMPACTS OF WILDLIFE TRAFFICKING AND BY CREATING SUITABLE HABITAT. SPECIFIC ACTIVITIES INCLUDE: (1) ESTABLISHING A BI-NATIONAL TECHNICAL GROUP FOR WILDLIFE TRAFFICKING TO COORDINATE AND IMPLEMENT THE EXISTING ENVIRONMENTAL PROTECTION STRATEGY BETWEEN THE TWO COUNTRIES AND STRENGTHEN THE EFFORTS OF LAW ENFORCEMENT IN ITS EFFICIENCY, CONTROL, AND SURVEILLANCE OPERATIONS (2) ESTABLISHING AGROFORESTRY PROJECTS TO RESTORE CROSS-BORDER ECOLOGICAL CONNECTIVITY AND PROMOTE SUSTAINABLE ECONOMIC ALTERNATIVES TO WILDLIFE TRAFFICKING AND (3) PROVIDING TECHNICAL ASSISTANCE FOR THE ENVIRONMENTAL EDUCATION PROGRAM EDUCATING FOR THE CONSERVATION OF PROTECTED AREAS AND BIOLOGICAL DIVERSITY (EDUCONAP) TO INCREASE THE VALUE THAT LOCALS PUT ON PROTECTED AREAS AND BIOLOGICAL DIVERSITY IN GUATEMALA.</narrative>
  </description>
